What Is a Request to Stop Collection Activity Agreement?
A Request to Stop Collection Activity Agreement is a formal legal document used to instruct a collection agency to stop pursuing payment for debts that are disputed, incorrectly assigned, or the result of identity theft. This agreement provides written notice to the collection agency and creates an official paper trail of your objection.

Using a draft Request to Cease Collection Activity Agreement from Legalgram can help put an end to repeated phone calls, collection notices, and harassment related to debts you do not owe.

